# Sukie (bouyonmusique.com, wave 15 parity, 2026-10-20)
# THIN CATALOGUE, DOCUMENTED NEWS FILE: one title is verified in the sources consulted, and no official artist page on the streaming platforms consulted was confirmed during this research, so sameAs stays empty and the track list carries that single verified title only.
# Sources used:
# - DOM767, article published 2023-03-29, opened 2026-10-20: Shane Edwards, popularly known as Sukie Burn Brain, Dominican rave artiste, back in Dominica after early release from Grenadian prison; sentenced to six months for touching a teenage girl inappropriately on December 26, 2022, released after four months for good behaviour; Acting Commissioner of Prisons Rupert Neckles quoted on the prison recordings and the plan to release songs detailing the prison experience; arrest before the Fire and Ice performance with Ridge at the National Cricket Stadium; indecent assault charge before Judge Teddy St. Louis in St. George; Richmond Hill prison; earlier threat and battery case in Dominica still pending before a Roseau magistrate court at that time.
# - Nice FM 104.3, opened 2026-10-20, reporting Grenada Broadcasting Network: Sukie, real name Shane Edwards, also Sukie Burn Brain, taken into custody on two counts of indecent assault; Fire and Ice, the ultimate Concert, at the Grenada National Cricket Stadium, with Mr Ridge and Shenseea also expected; September 2022 arrest in Dominica on battery and threats charges, bail a month later, trial expected to commence in the Roseau Magistrate court on December 6, 2022.
# - Caribbean Times, Grenada court report, opened 2026-10-20: 36 year old Dominican artiste Shane Sukie Burn Brain Edwards charged with one count of indecent assault, denied bail, remanded to Richmond Hill prison, maximum five years if convicted. The one count and two counts versions between reports are published here as a documented discrepancy, never merged.
# - Bajan Reporter, 2023-11, opened 2026-10-20, on Jael Joseph LIVE: her interview with controversial Bouyon artist Sukie Burn Brain amassed 25k views, with 1,000 people tuning in live. The word controversial is that article framing, attributed as such.
# - CAT Radio and CaribMagPlus, Bouyon Road March 2025 reports, opened 2026-10-20: recent releases by artists such as Sukie Burn Brain, Mr. Ridge, Kenny G, Reo and Signal Band named as the momentum behind the first Bouyon Road March title. No Sukie title is named in those reports.
# - Blaqrose Supreme podcast tracklist, opened 2026-10-20: Keks Mafia featuring Sukie Burn Brain, Say My Name. The only Sukie title verified title by title in the sources consulted.
# - TikTok clip by Sully Jacob, search result 2026-10-20: clip titled Sukie on Bouyon vs Soca plus How He Brought Bouyon Back (His Real Come-Up). Used only as the framing of a circulating clip of Sukie telling his own come up, attributed, never as an established fact about the genre.
# Note on the court record: this profile reports the published record with its sources and its dates, distinguishes charges from the one sentence reported by DOM767, and states plainly where the outcome of the Dominica case is not given by any source consulted. No victim is named in any source used, and none is named here.

